Note that these equations are linearly independent. Therefore, we can let a well-defined TaT_{a} denote the maximal value of fif_{i} satisfying System 3.6. By Lemma 3.14, for any solution with a≥3a\geq 3, we have f4≥fif_{4}\geq f_{i} for all ii. Therefore, Ta=f4T_{a}=f_{4} if a≥3a\geq 3. We claim that, for a≥3a\geq 3,
Ta>a​Ta−1.T_{a}>a\,T_{a-1}.
