Note that the transformation from MaM_{a} to Ma′M_{a}^{\prime} only requires adding positive multiples of rows to other rows, as each row and column of MaM_{a} contains only one positive entry. Also, note that the (2​a)(2a)th column of MaM_{a} differs from the (2​a−2)(2a-2)th column in only two ways: they are negations and |Ma2​a−3, 2​a|=|Ma2​a−3, 2​a−2|+1|M_{a}^{2a-3,\,2a}|=|M_{a}^{2a-3,\,2a-2}|+1. Therefore, |Ma′i, 2​a|≥|Ma′i, 2​a−2||M_{a}^{\prime i,\,2a}|\geq|M_{a}^{\prime i,\,2a-2}|.
