5 Future Directions
In Theorem 3.10, we provided a lower bound for the maximum period of a parallel chip-firing game on an orientation of KnK_{n} that is asymptotic to (n−1)!(n-1)!. Similarly, in Theorem 3.15, we showed that the maximum period of a parallel chip-firing game on an orientation of Ka,bK_{a,\,b} with a≤ba\leq b is at least asymptotic to a!a!. More challenging is the complete characterization of the possible periods of parallel chip-firing games on orientations of KnK_{n} or Ka,bK_{a,\,b}. In particular, we conjectured in Conjectures 3.8 and 3.13 that τ⁡(n)\tau(n) and τ⁡(a,b)\tau(a,\,b) are indeed asymptotic to (n−1)!(n-1)! and a!a!, respectively. Finally, we conjecture that limc→∞Tc​(D)\lim_{c\to\infty}T_{c}(D) is finite and well-defined for all directed graphs DD.
Conjecture 5.1.
For any directed graph DD, the quantity Tc​(D)T_{c}(D) is stable for very large cc. That is, there exists some TT and c0c_{0} such that TT is a possible period of any parallel chip-firing game on DD with cc chips for all c≥c0c\geq c_{0}.
For the useful orientations of complete and complete bipartite graphs, we conjecture also that limc→∞Tc​(D)=Tc′​(D)\lim_{c\to\infty}T_{c}(D)=T_{c^{\prime}}(D), where c′c^{\prime} are the specific values of cc defined in Theorems 3.10 and 3.15.
